From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 07:20:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: placed maps, ray tracing, timestamps and sparse
 resources

From mihawk-99/PS5_Mesa, squashed:

  8639134f26f radv/ps5: placed memory maps, and no claims the port has not earned
  6787bbded56 radv/ps5: report acceleration structures and ray queries
  d42b81c8daa radv/ps5: take the fixed-function traits from Mesa's GFX1013 model
  8406b615493 aco, radv/ps5: ray tracing pipelines through buffer scratch
  95eb7128f73 radv/ps5: capture and replay addresses
  c94770c1caf radv/ps5: calibrated timestamps from the GPU clock
  c9aec748225 vulkan: no raw monotonic time domain without CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW
  b8a10e9f0db radv/ps5: sparse resources over the platform's mappings
  b5d43f9af2b radv: sparse images bind a GPU page at a time at least
  2ae4551c9ab radv/ps5: 3D sparse residency
  e535075dab2 radv: the SMEM null PRT workaround only with PRT sparse binding
  472a9840209 radv/ps5: sparse descriptor buffers in the 32-bit window
  6a3962bf520 radv: dedicated sparse queue only with native timelines
  8014f6773cb aco: borrow into the scratch descriptor's high word right on restore
  30fcf1b9dd3 radv/ps5: the host model releases its window when the driver unloads
---
